      "content": "Religious conservatives argue that MAID violates the sanctity of life and the divine right to life, viewing death as a sacred mystery that only God controls. In contrast, religious liberals often frame MAID as a compassionate act of mercy that respects individual autonomy and alleviates suffering without denying the soul's value. While conservatives fear this legalizes euthanasia and erodes moral boundaries, liberals contend that refusing care for the dying is a greater sin than assisting a competent person in choosing their end. Ultimately, the debate hinges on whether the state should protect life at all costs or protect the dignity of those facing unbearable pain.",
